  "question": "Can a label's probability be read off a single token, as 3.2's wording implies and D7 consumes?",
  "verdict": "No for every multi-class subtask on at least one tokeniser. First-token distinctness holds everywhere and is not the relevant property; the relevant property is whether the first token is specific to its label, and it is not. The arm therefore scores full label sequences with length normalisation instead of reading a single token. See llm_protocol in configs/e2_matrix.yaml and THESIS_LOG #54.",
